WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:02.400
.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.920
- Double scotch.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.140
- Water chaser.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:45.840
- Yes, sir.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:30.000
sorry after you pack of cigarettes any brand anything tonight not trying to annoy you i just thought maybe

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:34.420
- They're no good to me. I've been stood up. - No, thank you.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:39.510
- It's a shame to waste them. It's a hit. - I know.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.820
- I thought maybe you could call a friend. - Pray not.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:56.380
- Don't suppose you'd go with me, would you? - Another one, sir?

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.740
No, never mind.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:14.710
- Well, how about it? - Yes. Yes, I'll go.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.510
Okay, let's go. It's late now. How much do we owe?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.720
- Oh, by the way, my name is... - Oh, no. No names, no addresses.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.040
Just companions for the evening. It's the only condition on which I'll go.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.340
Okay. Suits me.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.190
$1.60. Oh, a nickel.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.940
Keep it. Thanks.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:48.780
Care to smoke?

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:51.490
No, thank you.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:55.610
Do you live in New York?

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.330
Yes.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:00.000
Well, then they're useless.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.000
to this kind of weather.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.920
Yes.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:08.340
You know, there's something that gets me about this town on a hot Saturday night.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:14.750
Have you ever walked down Broadway and watched the people's faces?

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:19.150
It's fun.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.150
Now, there's a typical New York character for you.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:30.000
You know, back there in that bar, I felt pretty low, but riding away...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.660
Along here like this, I'd feel much better.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.680
Look, I'm afraid I'm not going to be very good company.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.090
Relax.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:44.030
You know, you shouldn't be alone any more than I should.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:45.950
Well, that's better.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:49.300
Now let's just have fun, and maybe the show is amusing.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.020
Yes.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.960
I hope so, too.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.610
I'd like to laugh.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.080
It would be fun to laugh.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.120
Everyone's movement is showin' improvement

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.320
with chicky chicky chicky chicky chicky cha

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.950
chicky chicky chicky chicky cha

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:24.310
Every morning it's movin' has fit in time

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:26.400
to this thrillable beat of each syllable

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.580
chicky chicky chicky chicky cha

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:29.540
My hat!

00:06:30.000 --> 00:07:00.000
Look at her face, she can murder you.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:17.180
Chiki-chiki-chiki-chiki-chiki-chiki-cham. Chiki-chiki-chiki-chiki-chiki-cham. If you're Brazilian, French or Castilian, then you're Sicilian, Spanish or Chilean. Bet you a million. You're a chiki-chiki-cham.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.150
- Well, here we are.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:35.960
- You've been very kind.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.680
Goodbye.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.780
- Why can't I buy you a night cab?

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:42.310
- I'd rather you didn't come in.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:45.370
- I must confess, I'd like to know who you are.

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:48.850
- No, it's better this way.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.120
Marcella, listen, Marcella, I know you're awake.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.170
I saw your bedroom light from downstairs.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.620
Now, come on, I want to talk to you.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:45.020
- Who are you?

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:46.130
- Well, who are you?

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:49.270
What do you want?

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:50.650
- Where's my wife?

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:52.220
- Marcella.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:53.800
- Say, what is this?

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.400
- What's up?

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.920
- Let me go in there.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:57.960
- All right, let him go in.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:55.040
- I'm Inspector Burgess.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:58.110
I'll have to ask you a few questions.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.510
Take all the time you want.

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:15.310
- I'm okay now.

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:18.450
- Mr. Henderson?

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:19.730
- 32.

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:21.980
- Her age?

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:23.110
- 29.

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:24.860
- Married long?

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:26.640
- Five years.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.250
- Your occupation?

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:30.000
- I'm an engineer.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:33.580
- Scott Henderson, Incorporated.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:38.820
- When was the last time you saw Mrs. Henderson?

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.300
- Around seven.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.570
- Did you have dinner at home?

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:44.100
- No.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:47.600
- You dined out with your wife?

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:50.330
- No, I intended taking her to dinner in the theater,

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:53.150
but she changed her mind, so I went without her.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:55.340
- That little squabble, huh?

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:56.740
- We had words, yes.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.030
- Nothing serious, though.

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:00.000
- No, for a long time,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.490
and things haven't been right between us.

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:05.160
It was our anniversary.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:08.800
I thought maybe we could start all over again, so...

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.470
I came home from the office early.

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:12.410
We had friends in for cocktails.

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:14.830
- Who were they? - Oh, there was Tommy Wilson,

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:19.320
a client of mine, and his wife, and Jack Marlow.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.350
He's my best friend. He was leaving for South America.

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:26.830
They didn't stay long, and she seemed glad that we were alone.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:29.060
She let me go ahead and shower and change,

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.150
and I noticed she wasn't getting dressed.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:35.680
She just sat there and laughed.

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:38.530
She told me she had no intention of going out with me.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:40.110
She kept laughing at me.

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:44.340
- Nothing makes a man sorer than that.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:46.650
- Then I knew I'd been kidding myself.

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:52.970
I knew it wouldn't work, so I asked her for a divorce.

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:54.350
- She refused?

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:57.010
- Yes, she said she wouldn't be my wife,

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:59.540
but she wouldn't give me a divorce.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:07.580
Don't say that. We've been happy once.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:15.110
It was just that she was too spoiled and too beautiful.

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:22.920
In there.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:39.080
I never saw a man so nervous.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:47.250
How would you be if you came home and found your wife at the...

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:11.880
Look what they're doing! Her hair along the floor.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:42.180
- I thought guys didn't cry.

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:45.270
- Where were you around eight o'clock tonight?

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:46.190
- In a bar.

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:47.390
- Alone?

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:49.860
- No, I met a woman that wasn't in the mood

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:53.810
to be by myself, so I asked her to go to a show with me.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.370
- Who was she?

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:58.140
- I don't know, she didn't tell me her name.

00:13:58.140 --> 00:13:59.180
- Well, she didn't.

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:00.000
Besides, what's that got to do?

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:07.210
to do with it very neat dresser mr. Henderson yes everything goes together

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:19.140
it's an art nice tie you're wearing high pretty taste expensive I wish I could

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:22.240
afford it say what are you trying to do to me

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:26.770
Marcella's dead give me a break what's the difference whether my ties okay or

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:30.000
not makes a great deal of difference mr.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:34.340
- Mr. Henderson, why?

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:37.480
Your wife was strangled with one of your ties.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.400
- Yeah, it knotted so tight,

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:51.560
it had to be cut loose with a knife.

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:54.660
- Good morning, Ruthie.

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:55.660
Is Mr. Henderson in yet?

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.550
- No, no, he's not.

00:14:57.550 --> 00:15:00.000
Bring your book, will you, Ruthie?

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:00.930
I want to get off.

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:02.700
Carol!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:13.590
Listen, I won't be in until noon.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.620
I have to get this old body of mine examined for insurance.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:19.760
Air mail those blueprints off to Stone.

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:22.430
Call up every second-hand bookstore in town

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:26.110
and try to find a back issue of Engineering for July 1935.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:27.530
You get that?

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:29.190
July 1935.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:31.570
There's an article I want.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.540
I can't think of anything else right now.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:36.060
Oh, yes.

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:37.970
You better catch...

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:05.860
Come on in, Ruthie. It's all right. I just saw it in the papers.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:10.050
I couldn't tell you myself. I was afraid you'd go all to pieces.

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:11.600
That would be too easy.

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:13.870
They say they're questioning him.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.470
It'll be all right. They haven't arrested him, Ruthie.

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:18.430
It's horrible for him, but he'll explain.

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:21.940
I hope so. I'm sick from thinking about it.

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:23.210
There's no reason to be upset.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:25.910
We'll just have to stay here and wait for him to call us.

00:16:26.070 --> 00:16:26.730
Go on working.

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:29.190
Let's try not to think about it anymore.

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:30.000
Okay, good.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.280
See, I guess the Stone letter comes first.

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:36.210
- Are you ready? - Yes.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:39.860
Irwin Stone Company, Cleveland, Ohio.

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:44.180
Dear Mr. Stone, under separate cover,

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:46.090
we are sending you a duplicate of the blueprints.

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:49.830
And we wish to assure you that...

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:53.660
- Where was I? - And we wish to assure you that...

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:59.510
Oh, yes. And we wish to assure you that...

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:05.480
The original estimate for the Garden and Terrace is the correct one.

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:15.420
I submitted to you on July 16th.

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:19.140
Funny you can remember the bar, but you can't remember what the woman was like.

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:21.210
We've been over that hundreds of times.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.280
- Leave me alone, I'm tired. - You're tired, eh?

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:28.790
Don't you realize that this can end up in an awful long risk cure for you unless you're...

00:17:28.890 --> 00:17:30.000
I've told you you're wasting your time.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.610
- You're trying to pin this on me. - Yeah, sure.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:37.930
Remarkable though, I was with a woman and you don't know who she is or what she looked like.

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:45.330
I've told you, she was about 30, she had sort of brown hair, she wore a funny hat, that's all I can remember.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:52.440
If you'd ask me sooner, last night before all this, I could've told you more about her, but now she's complete blank.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:59.890
- Oh, there he is. - What's the idea of getting me up at this hour? I only work the evening shift.

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:01.760
I'm Inspector Burgess Homicide.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.360
Did you ever see this man before?

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:08.710
To me, a face is a face.

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:10.570
Take a good look.

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:13.540
Sit on the same stool.

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:25.600
Come down here, try again.

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:27.560
Forget about me, look at him.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:34.980
It's gloomy Gus. Sometime last night, wasn't it?

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:35.980
There, you see.

00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:37.990
What time last night?

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:39.990
Well, my shift goes on at 8:00. He come in sometime after.

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:40.990
How much after 8:00?

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:45.200
I don't make people punch the time clock. Sometime after 8:00.

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:47.120
Ask him about her. She saw the time.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:49.490
How about the woman who was in here?

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:50.870
What woman?

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:52.350
But I was...

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:54.160
I'll do the talking.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:57.120
Are you sure there wasn't a woman sitting in the chair next to this man?

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:58.120
Sure, I'm sure.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:18:59.980
Why, she wore a crazy hat, you know.

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:02.150
I've been serving in bars for 30 years.

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:05.540
To me, a dame is just another order, another drink.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.740
Well, if you remember me, why can't you remember her?

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:09.280
Because you're sitting right here on my chin.

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:11.260
Bring the dame back and put her in front of me the same way,

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:12.300
and maybe I'll remember her.

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:13.580
But there are only the two of us.

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:16.520
Why, she played the jukebox, and we left her together.

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:17.360
All right, all right.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:19.970
She sat right there, and she spoke to you.

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:20.570
Come on, Henderson.

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:23.210
You must remember her.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:23.910
Come on.

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:58.870
Did you ever haul last night from a bar called Anselmo's to the casino theater?

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:06.650
A hacker picks him up and puts him down so many times during the night that from Anselmo's to the casino theater.

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:09.550
That's about a 45-cent run on a dry night.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:11.600
Yeah, I did.

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:13.080
Do you see him here?

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:17.160
I didn't hold no one in that shape last night.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.460
No offense meant.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:22.280
It was him, huh?

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:23.560
You tell us.

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:26.840
Yeah, him.

00:20:27.190 --> 00:20:27.830
Was he alone?

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.500
- I think so.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.090
- But there was a woman with me.

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:35.600
You must have seen her.

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:38.460
- Hacking for eight years gives a guy a memory.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:41.400
If you was with a woman, I'd have noticed.

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:43.120
- Thanks, Alp.

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:46.920
You sure?

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:49.340
- Sure.

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:54.450
There was no dame with this guy in my cab last night.

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:55.510
- Come on, Henderson.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.930
Mr. Saunders, who are these men?

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:08.790
I must change.

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:10.980
This is Inspector Burgess. He'd like to talk to you.

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:14.900
Miss Montero, do you remember a woman sitting with this man last night wearing a hat like yours?

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:20.230
A hat like mine? Oh, really, this is too funny. No woman wears hats like mine.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:23.350
But she did. And you kept looking at her.

00:21:23.350 --> 00:21:26.350
No, no, go away. This is really funny.

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:30.000
No, no, go away. This is really funny.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.090
I'm an artist. I sing. I dance.

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:34.970
I don't look at my audience.

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:42.760
What woman besides Montero could wear those

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:45.760
and not look like how you say "ridiculo"?

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:46.760
Do you see the hat?

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:47.650
No.

00:21:47.650 --> 00:21:50.480
Miss Montero is only substantiating what I've told you.

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:51.590
You're lying.

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:53.730
No! Get him out!

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:59.410
Told you not to get pistachio.

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:00.780
How's yours?

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:02.980
Never go wrong on vanilla.

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:09.770
Why don't you admit there wasn't any woman with you last night?

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:10.470
No.

00:22:10.980 --> 00:22:13.700
If I did that, I'd never be sure of anything again in my life.

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:15.930
She sat at the bar with me.

00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:18.850
Liked a certain tune and played it on a jukebox.

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:21.280
We walked down 46th Street together.

00:22:22.600 --> 00:22:23.240
She was real.

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:27.180
She was real.

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:30.000
And now you're trying to tell me she never existed.

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:36.900
- Where to now, Chief? - Some place where we can give him a drink.

00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:42.990
We all need a drink. Then drive back to headquarters.

00:22:44.340 --> 00:22:48.100
- She'd better get some sleep. - Yeah, and a good lawyer.

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:51.250
He's gonna need both.

00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:59.500
Marcella Henderson met her death at three minutes after eight.

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:04.100
The prosecution accepts this as a fact.

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:10.490
Now, the defense claims that Scott Henderson was with a woman at Anselmo's bar four miles

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:16.300
away from his home at five minutes after eight, on the night the murder was committed.

00:23:16.300 --> 00:23:19.030
Very clever.

00:23:19.030 --> 00:23:23.470
The defense also asks you to believe that if he was at Anselmo's bar at five minutes

00:23:23.470 --> 00:23:30.000
after eight, then he couldn't possibly have been in his own apartment two minutes before.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:41.740
his wife was murdered again I say very clever but not clever enough witnesses

00:23:41.740 --> 00:23:45.280
who were at the same places and at the same time that Scott Henderson claims to

00:23:45.280 --> 00:23:51.050
have been with this woman can recall seeing him yet not one of them remembers

00:23:51.050 --> 00:23:59.010
her where is this woman has any of us seen her has she at any time been on that

00:23:59.010 --> 00:24:00.000
witness stand

00:24:02.970 --> 00:24:09.280
Of course not. Because there is no such woman. There never was.

00:24:09.280 --> 00:24:15.760
Mr. Henderson, you say you were with this woman for several hours.

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:19.340
What did you call her?

00:24:19.340 --> 00:24:22.540
I just called her you.

00:24:22.540 --> 00:24:27.270
Well, can't you tell us anything about her?

00:24:27.270 --> 00:24:30.000
Was she a blonde, brunette, tall, short, or what?

00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:40.620
i don't know i can't remember believe me your honor i'm telling the truth in a blind rage he

00:24:40.620 --> 00:24:46.140
took the necktie which he had in his hands dropped it around her throat and tightened it with

00:24:46.140 --> 00:25:00.000
unimaginable cruelty until it was so embedded in her soft flesh that it had to be cut off will the accused please

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.360
Please rise and face the jury.

00:25:02.890 --> 00:25:06.620
Will the foreman of the jury please stand?

00:25:07.360 --> 00:25:10.460
Ladies and gentlemen of the jury, have you reached a verdict?

00:25:10.640 --> 00:25:13.500
We have, Your Honor.

00:25:14.780 --> 00:25:18.520
Do you find the defendant guilty or not guilty of the charge made against him?

00:25:21.870 --> 00:25:23.640
I didn't hear the verdict. What was it?

00:25:23.740 --> 00:25:26.020
What did you expect? Guilty.

00:25:42.030 --> 00:25:44.440
- Hello, Mr. Henderson. - Hello, Kansas.

00:25:44.520 --> 00:25:47.250
They give you five minutes.

00:25:47.330 --> 00:25:49.810
Is there anything I can do for you?

00:25:49.890 --> 00:25:57.560
Yes, you can thank the foreman. I forgot to.

00:25:57.640 --> 00:26:00.000
- I don't know what to say. - It's skipping.

00:26:00.030 --> 00:26:06.850
Kansas I'll be all right now that I know where I stand yes I'll be fine last night for the first

00:26:06.850 --> 00:26:12.740
time I didn't have to count sheep I slept like a guilty man but you're going to appeal with what

00:26:12.740 --> 00:26:23.440
a set of blueprints and my grandfather's watch question money oh Kansas no thanks it isn't the

00:26:23.440 --> 00:26:30.000
money we've done everything hired a flock of detectives bought time on the radio advertised

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.000
everything possible was done to find her.

00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:34.020
What about your friends? Won't they help?

00:26:34.020 --> 00:26:36.100
Oh, yes. Remember all my friends?

00:26:36.100 --> 00:26:37.100
Well, they aren't.

00:26:37.100 --> 00:26:40.030
Haven't you heard from Mr. Marlowe?

00:26:40.030 --> 00:26:43.660
No, I didn't let him know.

00:26:43.660 --> 00:26:46.150
He's your best friend. It looks like it.

00:26:46.150 --> 00:26:47.980
He'd be the one to help him.

00:26:47.980 --> 00:26:49.980
I didn't want to drag him back from South America.

00:26:49.980 --> 00:26:52.220
That's his big chance down there.

00:26:52.220 --> 00:26:54.970
In any case, what good could he do?

00:26:54.970 --> 00:27:00.000
I don't know. But you need someone to help you who really is.

00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:02.140
Someone who just won't be beaten.

00:27:02.140 --> 00:27:06.170
Stop blowing bubbles, Kansas.

00:27:06.170 --> 00:27:11.360
But you can't let that verdict stand, Mr. Henderson.

00:27:11.360 --> 00:27:13.360
You've got to fight.

00:27:13.360 --> 00:27:15.220
But I told you, it's no use.

00:27:15.220 --> 00:27:17.370
You were at the trial. I don't blame the jury.

00:27:17.370 --> 00:27:22.820
If I were in the jury box, I'd have agreed with him.

00:27:22.820 --> 00:27:25.860
But somebody has to go on looking for her.

00:27:25.860 --> 00:27:29.130
You know, being shut up alone so much...

00:27:30.990 --> 00:27:34.590
I've been thinking. Maybe there never was such a woman.

00:27:34.590 --> 00:27:36.800
It's just my word against theirs.

00:27:36.800 --> 00:27:39.920
Maybe I just imagined it. Maybe she doesn't exist.

00:27:39.920 --> 00:27:42.240
Stop talking like that.

00:27:42.240 --> 00:27:47.320
You can't work for a man as long as I work for you and not know him pretty well.

00:27:47.320 --> 00:27:50.760
You couldn't kill anybody.

00:27:50.760 --> 00:27:54.690
Thanks, Kansas. That makes you a minority of one.

00:27:54.690 --> 00:27:59.960
Time's up. Are you going back to Wichita?

00:28:02.940 --> 00:28:04.860
- I haven't decided what to do yet.

00:28:04.860 --> 00:28:07.630
- Well, whoever you work for, I'll be a pretty lucky boss.

00:28:07.630 --> 00:28:09.350
If you keep your bobby pins off the floor

00:28:09.350 --> 00:28:11.370
and the seams in your stockings straight.

00:28:11.370 --> 00:28:16.270
If you don't, he'll fire you.

00:28:16.270 --> 00:28:23.770
Goodbye, Kansas.

00:28:23.770 --> 00:28:26.510
- Oh, if you feel like a train ride, visit me sometime.

00:28:26.510 --> 00:28:28.160
I'm getting a new address tomorrow.

00:28:28.160 --> 00:28:29.800
A big country estate on the Hudson.

00:28:30.160 --> 00:28:36.210
On a clear day, you can see New Jersey.

00:28:36.210 --> 00:28:39.980
- Goodbye, Kansas. - Goodbye, Mr. Henderson.

00:28:39.980 --> 00:28:53.360
Here's the horse I like, third race, Pimlico.

00:28:53.360 --> 00:28:55.320
No, I like Sergeant Mike in the third.

00:28:55.320 --> 00:28:58.370
- Customer man. - Are you crazy, Sergeant?

00:28:58.370 --> 00:29:00.000
You know, Sergeant Mike hasn't won

00:29:00.120 --> 00:29:02.200
- Yeah, but do you know he's ready right now?

00:29:02.200 --> 00:29:03.240
- Why, he's at the door.

00:29:03.240 --> 00:29:05.690
- I'd like to bet on women's side.

00:29:05.690 --> 00:29:06.870
- Yes, miss?

00:29:06.870 --> 00:29:13.250
- Pinch bottle and water.

00:29:33.160 --> 00:29:35.820
You bettin' high girl second race tomorrow?

00:29:35.820 --> 00:29:37.800
Hey, Mac, we're talkin' to ya.

00:29:37.800 --> 00:29:40.240
You got any money on that filly tomorrow?

00:29:40.240 --> 00:29:42.480
Oh, yeah, yeah, ten bucks on the nose.

00:29:42.480 --> 00:29:43.920
- Ten bucks? - Eight dollars.

00:29:43.920 --> 00:29:46.040
- Where does he get the dough? - He does.

00:29:46.040 --> 00:29:50.510
Callin' that guy.

00:29:50.510 --> 00:29:52.930
Don't you care for your drink, miss?

00:29:52.930 --> 00:29:54.680
Everything is fine.

00:29:54.680 --> 00:29:57.840
Mac, another beer.

00:29:57.840 --> 00:30:00.000
No, you got a problem trying to lose.

00:30:46.000 --> 00:30:47.000
- I'll play. - Fine.

00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:48.470
Mac, give me my hat and coat, will ya?

00:30:48.470 --> 00:30:57.250
I've been sitting there all night, like last night and the night before, staring at me.

00:30:57.250 --> 00:30:59.830
Sure, she keeps staring at you. She wants another drink.

00:31:04.350 --> 00:31:15.110
Closing up, miss. Closing up, miss.

00:34:50.250 --> 00:34:51.350
What's the trouble, mister?

00:34:51.350 --> 00:34:53.070
You think you're smart, don't you?

00:34:53.070 --> 00:34:53.970
I'm on to you.

00:34:53.970 --> 00:34:55.030
Is he bothering you, miss?

00:34:55.030 --> 00:34:56.030
No, no. It's all right.

00:34:56.030 --> 00:34:57.240
He's a lush, huh?

00:34:57.240 --> 00:34:59.250
Please keep out of this. This is between us.

00:35:00.380 --> 00:35:03.660
- You've got something to tell me. - You're wasting your time.

00:35:03.760 --> 00:35:07.080
You know what's going to happen to him, don't you? You can prevent it.

00:35:07.310 --> 00:35:09.430
You don't want that on your conscience, do you?

00:35:09.530 --> 00:35:11.850
- If you want me to, I'll... - No, don't interfere.

00:35:11.950 --> 00:35:14.400
- Okay, lady. - Well?

00:35:14.500 --> 00:35:18.360
I ain't talking, see? You ain't got nothing on me. Nothing.

00:35:18.490 --> 00:35:21.620
If you want to find out anything, ask the guy who give it to me.

00:35:21.810 --> 00:35:25.070
- Who bribed you? - I...

00:35:25.170 --> 00:35:29.720
Wait a minute. Let me go! Take your hands off me!

00:36:12.890 --> 00:36:16.240
- How did you get in here? - Your landlady. Remember me?

00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:19.450
I'm a tired police inspector named Burgess.

00:36:19.450 --> 00:36:22.820
If you're looking for Mr. Henderson, you'll find him just where you put him.

00:36:22.820 --> 00:36:24.930
Oh, come on now. That's nonsense and you know it.

00:36:24.930 --> 00:36:28.130
My job was done when I turned him over to the D.A.

00:36:28.130 --> 00:36:30.000
So easy.

00:36:30.060 --> 00:36:34.270
- It's easy to be smug and wear a badge on your mind, isn't it?

00:36:34.270 --> 00:36:48.320
You must feel very proud of yourself.

00:36:48.320 --> 00:36:53.500
- Found a new job yet?

00:36:53.500 --> 00:36:56.350
Why don't you go home to Kansas?

00:36:56.350 --> 00:36:58.710
- I'm staying here, I've things to do.

00:37:00.190 --> 00:37:05.160
- Like going around frightening bar men?

00:37:05.160 --> 00:37:08.700
That's what I'm paid for, to know those things.

00:37:08.700 --> 00:37:12.800
Why did you follow him?

00:37:12.800 --> 00:37:14.960
- Maybe I needed the exercise.

00:37:14.960 --> 00:37:17.940
- Try Central Park next time, the air's better.

00:37:17.940 --> 00:37:19.790
- I don't have to tell you anything.

00:37:19.790 --> 00:37:22.520
- Maybe not, but what business is it of yours

00:37:22.520 --> 00:37:24.700
to go around and-- - It isn't in my business.

00:37:24.700 --> 00:37:26.750
But he hasn't anyone else to fight for him.

00:37:26.750 --> 00:37:29.050
He won't appeal, he has no money, no friends.

00:37:31.950 --> 00:37:38.970
- I had to do something. - He could have come to me.

00:37:39.350 --> 00:37:42.800
You forget, Inspector. I know Scott's innocent.

00:37:43.380 --> 00:37:49.040
- So do I. - What do you mean?

00:37:50.850 --> 00:37:55.310
I won't say I did my job poorly. The evidence shoved him right into the chair.

00:37:55.560 --> 00:38:00.000
But since the trial, I've been doing a lot of thinking. The only defense Scott

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:03.300
was to continually talk about a woman with a funny hat.

00:38:03.400 --> 00:38:05.920
My kid could have done a better job of describing it.

00:38:06.020 --> 00:38:10.980
No, only a fool or an innocent man would have stuck to that alibi.

00:38:11.080 --> 00:38:13.290
A guilty man would have been smarter.

00:38:13.390 --> 00:38:16.800
Scott wasn't being smart. He was telling the truth.

00:38:16.900 --> 00:38:22.240
The case is closed officially, but I'd like to help unofficially.

00:38:22.340 --> 00:38:25.190
Well, how about it?

00:39:48.940 --> 00:39:50.950
You could have knocked me cold when you gave me the eye.

00:39:50.950 --> 00:39:52.770
Gee, you sure know how to beat it out.

00:39:52.770 --> 00:39:53.690
Thanks, baby.

00:39:53.690 --> 00:39:55.690
Oh, by the way, the handle's Cliff.

00:39:55.690 --> 00:39:56.690
Cliff Milbeth.

00:39:56.690 --> 00:39:57.690
I'm Jeannie.

00:39:57.690 --> 00:39:59.620
You and I are going to have fun tonight.

00:39:59.620 --> 00:40:00.000
Let's go.

00:40:00.770 --> 00:40:02.650
- Do you like jive? - You bet.

00:40:02.850 --> 00:40:05.090
- I'm a half kitten. - Oh, baby.

00:43:25.080 --> 00:43:26.880
Are you just gonna stand there? What are you looking at?

00:43:26.880 --> 00:43:28.630
It's just a room.

00:43:28.630 --> 00:43:29.630
Gee, Cliff.

00:43:31.880 --> 00:43:36.090
- With all the dough you make? - My dough goes out other things, baby.

00:43:37.110 --> 00:43:40.650
Five and ten. I'll get you something better.

00:43:40.730 --> 00:43:46.640
- Will you, Cliff? Will you? Honest? - Just name it.

00:43:46.980 --> 00:43:51.260
What do you want, baby? I could make you look class.

00:43:52.120 --> 00:43:56.560
- That's cheap. - I suppose you don't like my hat, neither.

00:43:57.470 --> 00:43:58.890
Nah.

00:44:00.480 --> 00:44:03.480
Stick to me, Snooks. I'll stake you to a carload of hats.

00:44:03.600 --> 00:44:05.520
Oh, Cliff, you're sweet.

00:44:06.510 --> 00:44:09.150
I bet you wouldn't even know what sort of hat would look good on me.

00:44:09.450 --> 00:44:13.220
Me? I'm an authority on hats.

00:44:13.630 --> 00:44:15.690
I get paid for knowing about hats.

00:44:16.810 --> 00:44:17.490
Yeah, Cliff?

00:44:18.330 --> 00:44:18.770
Yeah.

00:44:19.680 --> 00:44:22.960
You can tell me. Ain't I your friend, huh?

00:44:26.400 --> 00:44:26.780
Yeah.

00:44:36.080 --> 00:44:39.540
Listen, Cliff, you get paid. Why?

00:44:39.630 --> 00:44:44.310
Why? There was a woman sitting in the front row.

00:44:44.610 --> 00:44:48.910
500 smackaroos just for looking at a dame and saying I didn't.

00:44:49.410 --> 00:44:55.600
- Tell me about it, Cliff. - Forget it.

00:44:56.130 --> 00:44:59.540
- Did she give you the 500, Cliff? - Nah.

00:45:00.250 --> 00:45:03.440
- Who gave it to you? - Some man.

00:45:04.530 --> 00:45:11.330
- Wait a minute, Cliff. What did the man say? - All right, that's for you, he says.

00:45:11.530 --> 00:45:14.880
All of it. 500 bucks if you say there was no damn.

00:45:15.060 --> 00:45:18.460
No matter who has you, say no. Keep on saying no.

00:45:18.800 --> 00:45:19.780
And then he beat it.

00:45:20.750 --> 00:45:23.010
- Give me a cigarette, Jeannie. - I haven't any.

00:45:38.120 --> 00:45:40.390
That's me. Everything about me.

00:45:41.560 --> 00:45:43.940
They sent you. Somebody's after me.

00:45:45.310 --> 00:45:47.030
And you made me believe you like me.

00:45:47.190 --> 00:45:48.910
I do. Yeah, I do, Cliff.

00:45:49.270 --> 00:45:49.910
Don't you remember?

00:45:50.320 --> 00:45:52.460
I was sitting in your lap. I was kissing you.

00:45:52.460 --> 00:45:53.960
You made me believe you like me.

00:45:54.360 --> 00:45:54.600
What?

00:46:08.410 --> 00:46:09.090
Where are you?

00:46:36.560 --> 00:46:39.010
- Your phone? - Yes. There.

00:46:39.030 --> 00:46:42.860
What's the matter, miss? You have any problems?

00:46:42.900 --> 00:46:44.840
Come out front.

00:46:44.940 --> 00:46:56.970
Oh, Mr. Burgess. No. No, I'm all right. But hurry.

00:46:56.980 --> 00:47:00.000
- I'm in... what store? - Joseph's.

00:47:00.700 --> 00:47:02.910
Joseph's delicatessen, just as I was at his house.

00:47:03.390 --> 00:47:06.560
- How long will it take you? - Oh, good.

00:47:08.480 --> 00:47:11.620
Do you have troubles? Maybe I can help you.

00:47:11.700 --> 00:47:14.950
Don't ask Angela's mama. I fixed some coffee for you.

00:47:17.290 --> 00:47:25.090
- Who's that? - It's only me, Cliff.

00:47:30.480 --> 00:47:32.560
What a place. I feel the rats in the walls.

00:47:32.560 --> 00:47:35.510
What'd you come here for?

00:47:35.510 --> 00:47:37.540
It's good to sit down again.

00:47:37.540 --> 00:47:40.680
I've been standing for hours on the sidewalk while you drummed away.

00:47:40.680 --> 00:47:41.590
Listen, mister.

00:47:41.590 --> 00:47:44.780
I wish I'd been in the room with you while you were playing, Cliff.

00:47:44.780 --> 00:47:46.700
You're a fine technician.

00:47:46.700 --> 00:47:50.000
It was an exciting girl you took there with you.

00:47:50.000 --> 00:47:50.930
Girl?

00:47:50.930 --> 00:47:56.660
Yeah. Brought her here.

00:47:56.660 --> 00:47:59.990
Genie. She's... She's...

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:01.000
She's okay.

00:48:01.000 --> 00:48:02.000
She was magnificent.

00:48:02.000 --> 00:48:05.870
She loathed you, but she went with you.

00:48:05.870 --> 00:48:10.100
She would have humiliated herself to make you talk.

00:48:10.100 --> 00:48:11.500
I didn't tell her anything.

00:48:11.500 --> 00:48:13.500
Why lie, Cliff?

00:48:13.500 --> 00:48:16.480
You can have back your 500 bucks.

00:48:16.480 --> 00:48:20.060
Don't come near me, please.

00:48:20.060 --> 00:48:24.600
What are you thinking about?

00:48:24.600 --> 00:48:27.840
Oh, how interesting a pair of hands can be.

00:48:27.840 --> 00:48:30.000
They can trick me.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.000
melody out of a piano keyboard.

00:48:32.000 --> 00:48:36.890
They can mold beauty out of a piece of common clay.

00:48:36.890 --> 00:48:41.720
They can bring life back to a dying child.

00:48:41.720 --> 00:48:47.440
Yeah, a pair of hands can do inconceivable good.

00:48:47.440 --> 00:48:52.750
Yet the same pair of hands can do terrible evil.

00:48:52.750 --> 00:48:58.520
They can destroy, torture, even kill.

00:49:01.560 --> 00:49:27.050
I wish I didn't have to use my hands to hurt another human being.

00:49:27.050 --> 00:49:30.000
It's coming so soon. He saw her. Somebody bribed him.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:32.100
- I have a warrant already in my pocket. - I'm going with you.

00:49:32.100 --> 00:49:34.760
- No, you stay in the store. You've been through enough. - No, no.

00:49:34.760 --> 00:49:55.000
- This time it's no accident. - But we have proof now.

00:49:55.000 --> 00:49:59.480
- He told me that he... - It's no good, Carol. They won't accept it. He's dead.

00:50:16.670 --> 00:50:18.740
- How are you? - I'm fine.

00:50:19.200 --> 00:50:22.600
I've gained weight, fattening me up for the slaughter.

00:50:22.940 --> 00:50:25.280
I've got a date in 18 days.

00:50:25.840 --> 00:50:29.190
- But your appeal? - It's denied.

00:50:30.860 --> 00:50:32.600
Oh, stop feeling sorry for me.

00:50:35.130 --> 00:50:36.670
I'm not very sociable these days,

00:50:36.730 --> 00:50:38.580
but you happen to be the only one

00:50:38.580 --> 00:50:39.600
that comes up here to see me.

00:50:40.550 --> 00:50:42.290
You needn't apologize, Mr. Henderson.

00:50:42.680 --> 00:50:43.960
I understand.

00:50:44.900 --> 00:50:45.620
Mr. Henderson.

00:50:46.350 --> 00:50:47.770
Even the guards call me Scott.

00:50:48.990 --> 00:50:49.710
And another thing.

00:50:50.310 --> 00:50:51.950
Last week, we kept talking about me.

00:50:52.400 --> 00:50:53.320
Let's not this time.

00:50:53.800 --> 00:50:55.160
Let's talk about anything else.

00:50:57.170 --> 00:50:58.090
You pick the subject.

00:50:59.340 --> 00:51:00.000
You don't have to.

00:51:00.030 --> 00:51:01.920
You can't talk at all unless you want to.

00:51:01.920 --> 00:51:05.720
Serves you right for coming up here.

00:51:05.720 --> 00:51:07.220
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:51:07.220 --> 00:51:09.230
I didn't mean what I said.

00:51:09.230 --> 00:51:12.420
I just took it out on you.

00:51:12.420 --> 00:51:15.710
As a matter of fact, I'm always darned glad to see you.

00:51:15.710 --> 00:51:18.680
You oughtn't to waste your time coming up here.

00:51:18.680 --> 00:51:20.700
You oughtn't to be out having fun with some fella.

00:51:20.700 --> 00:51:24.000
Don't tell me you're not in love, Kansas.

00:51:24.000 --> 00:51:30.000
Well, for Pete's sake.

00:51:30.700 --> 00:51:37.780
- I hit the nail right on the head. Who is he? - My boss.

00:51:37.940 --> 00:51:43.380
Your boss? Well, that was quick. Didn't even know you had another job.

00:51:44.520 --> 00:51:46.260
So you've fallen for each other, huh?

00:51:49.090 --> 00:51:52.920
Gosh, that's fine. Yeah, that's fine.

00:51:55.120 --> 00:51:58.470
Guess I'd better go.

00:52:02.360 --> 00:52:06.920
- He'll come back again, won't you, Kansas? - Yes, Scott.

00:52:13.140 --> 00:52:14.920
Warden gave permission for another visitor.

00:52:17.910 --> 00:52:21.410
- Jack! Jack Marlowe! - Scotty.

00:52:23.770 --> 00:52:26.310
- Gosh, I'm glad to see you. - When did you get here?

00:52:26.590 --> 00:52:28.420
I just got in this morning. I flew in.

00:52:28.880 --> 00:52:30.000
Hello, Miss Richmond.

00:52:30.030 --> 00:52:32.830
- Hello, Mr. Marlowe. - Scotty.

00:52:32.910 --> 00:52:39.880
It was such a shock reading about it way down there.

00:52:39.920 --> 00:52:42.230
6,000 miles away.

00:52:42.230 --> 00:52:43.960
Scott didn't want you to know.

00:52:43.960 --> 00:52:47.510
He said your assignment in Brazil meant so much to you.

00:52:47.570 --> 00:52:54.020
- Is that part of it? - Yeah.

00:52:54.100 --> 00:52:58.700
- It's for a park in Rio. - Great strength.

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:02.440
What are you working on now?

00:53:02.440 --> 00:53:04.610
I haven't worked in months.

00:53:04.610 --> 00:53:07.690
Everything in the studio was done before.

00:53:07.690 --> 00:53:09.950
Before I went to South America.

00:53:09.950 --> 00:53:12.930
You only knew how much you're coming back, Mr. Scott.

00:53:12.930 --> 00:53:14.530
He said there were three or four people

00:53:14.530 --> 00:53:16.130
who could prove where he was that night.

00:53:16.130 --> 00:53:19.100
Have you tried them all?

00:53:19.100 --> 00:53:21.460
There's only Montero left.

00:53:21.460 --> 00:53:22.460
She's our last hope.

00:53:22.460 --> 00:53:26.390
When her show closes tonight, she's leaving tomorrow.

00:53:26.390 --> 00:53:29.480
If we don't get to her, I don't know what we'll do.

00:53:29.480 --> 00:53:30.000
The first thing,

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:35.460
you ought to do young ladies go back to kansas and get a rest from all this i can't i can't think

00:53:35.460 --> 00:53:42.370
of anything else you'll wear yourself out careful look this is a man's job i'm sorry but i just

00:53:42.370 --> 00:53:49.020
can't sit by that woman must be someplace in the city one word from her and scott would walk out

00:53:49.020 --> 00:54:00.000
a free man i tell you carol i'm afraid let's not worry about me don't you see we must get to this

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:05.800
- He would kill her if he ever found her. - Yes, I think he would.

00:54:05.900 --> 00:54:09.840
- I suppose he'd even kill me. - Don't say that.

00:54:09.940 --> 00:54:15.890
Do you think I'd care? Do you think I'd want to live as Gu...

00:54:15.990 --> 00:54:21.340
I used to watch her sitting at your desk, the way you looked at him.

00:54:21.440 --> 00:54:25.910
You saw what they've done to him. Twisted him. Hurt him so.

00:54:26.010 --> 00:54:30.000
He had such plans to build model cities. Sunlight in every room.

00:54:30.830 --> 00:54:34.650
Children's play yards everywhere for everyone.

00:54:35.290 --> 00:54:40.080
He hated to let anyone know how soft he really was, but he didn't fool me.

00:54:40.980 --> 00:54:43.000
And now they've made him bitter and hard.

00:54:43.440 --> 00:54:45.560
And he's not that way. You know that.

00:54:47.300 --> 00:54:51.930
I'm sorry I let myself go.

00:54:53.370 --> 00:54:55.130
Please don't ever tell him.

00:54:55.440 --> 00:54:58.640
It seemed so desperate for him. Only 18 days.

00:55:00.380 --> 00:55:02.830
I just don't know what to do.

00:55:02.830 --> 00:55:07.100
Someone, whoever it is, always gets there first.

00:55:07.100 --> 00:55:08.500
He's so clever.

00:55:08.500 --> 00:55:11.120
- Yes, there's genius behind such audacity.

00:55:11.120 --> 00:55:19.170
- No, only madness.

00:55:19.170 --> 00:55:23.120
- Madness is a frightening word.

00:55:23.120 --> 00:55:26.330
- What else can you call it, to go on killing?

00:55:26.330 --> 00:55:30.000
- Perhaps he hates to kill, perhaps he feels

00:55:30.280 --> 00:55:40.610
horror i don't care what he feels all i want to do is find that woman i back this show because i

00:55:40.610 --> 00:55:48.180
believed in it and i owe it success to all you children after tonight we go our separate ways

00:55:48.180 --> 00:55:53.160
but we shall carry with us the memory of a real partnership in tinsel and grease paint

00:55:54.350 --> 00:56:00.000
bless you and thank you for making this show a hit now let's all have fun

00:56:14.880 --> 00:56:15.830
What happened?

00:56:15.830 --> 00:56:16.830
I couldn't get anywhere with her.

00:56:16.830 --> 00:56:18.940
Are you sure she didn't recognize you?

00:56:18.940 --> 00:56:19.940
Positive.

00:56:19.940 --> 00:56:22.340
She thought I was one of the stagehands.

00:56:22.340 --> 00:56:25.340
She'd only admit that our woman wore a hat like hers that night, but she won't.

00:56:25.340 --> 00:56:26.290
She's too vague.

00:56:26.290 --> 00:56:28.420
I never even had a chance to mention the subject.

00:56:28.420 --> 00:56:30.000
Maybe you used the wrong technique.

00:56:30.060 --> 00:56:48.090
me, conspector. I guess I'm not the romantic type. It's very funny. Miss Montero, I thought I'd better tell you, the airport just called to say they couldn't get reservations on the 1030 plane. You'll have to take the 7 o'clock.

00:56:48.580 --> 00:57:00.000
Ora bolas, it's impossible. Ask them how can I get my sleep. That's the only reservation they can give you. Very well. I'll sacrifice myself and you can leave later by

00:57:00.120 --> 00:57:09.210
only we could have gotten the name of a milliner if if i'm fed up with that word if we knew where

00:57:09.210 --> 00:57:14.630
it was if we knew who made it if we knew the color you've never talked like that before did you ever

00:57:14.630 --> 00:57:19.670
see a chipmunk in a cage running round and round in a wheel that's me i think i'll get good and

00:57:19.670 --> 00:57:25.640
drunk well that's not a bad idea can i get you something carol no thank you

00:57:34.220 --> 00:57:39.860
And Barrymore said to me, "Claude, you are the greatest Polonius of your day."

00:57:39.860 --> 00:57:40.820
Really?

00:58:15.260 --> 00:58:23.330
- Marlowe, you startled me. The lights aren't working. - You can see she's never been in a dressing room before.

00:58:37.360 --> 00:58:41.520
- I could have told you everything had been moved out. - But I'd find something here.

00:58:42.550 --> 00:58:52.770
Let's go home. I never knew how dreary an empty theater could be.

00:58:53.770 --> 00:58:56.050
- Coming, Mono? - Can you wait a minute, Inspector?

00:58:56.130 --> 00:58:57.650
I've never had a chance to talk to you.

00:59:00.250 --> 00:59:04.830
Poor Carol. She doesn't know what it means to give up, does she?

00:59:04.830 --> 00:59:07.500
You know, at first, I thought it would be a cinch.

00:59:07.500 --> 00:59:11.100
Just get the lowdown on everybody-- friends, relatives, so I did.

00:59:11.100 --> 00:59:12.200
Even you, Marlowe.

00:59:12.200 --> 00:59:14.410
Gee, I was in mid-ocean when it happened.

00:59:14.410 --> 00:59:19.010
Yes, SS Vulcania sailed Thursday, August the 2nd, 8:30 p.m.

00:59:19.010 --> 00:59:22.810
Stateroom C, middle deck, arrived Rio, August the 15th.

00:59:22.810 --> 00:59:24.510
What an incredible memory.

00:59:24.510 --> 00:59:27.120
A lot of good it does me.

00:59:27.120 --> 00:59:30.000
No, no, the fact remains that none of you could have committed

00:59:30.320 --> 00:59:40.900
murders. Why not? You're all too normal. Oh, must be normal enough. He's just clever,

00:59:40.900 --> 00:59:51.110
that's all. Yes, all of them are diabolically clever. Who? Paranoics. That's simply your

00:59:51.110 --> 01:00:00.000
opinion. Psychiatrists might disagree. No, I've met paranoics before. They all have incredible

01:00:00.060 --> 01:00:07.900
egos, abnormal cunning, a contempt for life. Make him sound unbeatable. Oh, he doesn't worry me.

01:00:08.760 --> 01:00:15.940
It's just that there's so little time left. Can't ask help from anyone, officially. My hands are

01:00:15.940 --> 01:00:23.550
tied, but I'll get the murderer sooner or later. It's always simpler when they're insane. Are you

01:00:23.550 --> 01:00:29.380
sure it isn't sour grapes, Inspector? Maybe he's more astute than we are, but to call him

01:00:30.510 --> 01:00:31.710
I'd stake my life on it.

01:00:32.770 --> 01:00:33.510
Might lose.

01:00:33.950 --> 01:00:34.950
No, I won't lose.

01:00:35.790 --> 01:00:37.750
We used to talk about the criminal type.

01:00:38.750 --> 01:00:40.130
Criminal type, my eye.

01:00:40.430 --> 01:00:41.690
It's not how a man looks.

01:00:41.890 --> 01:00:43.970
It's how his mind works that makes him a killer.

01:00:44.170 --> 01:00:45.620
Oh, come on, Inspector.

01:00:45.820 --> 01:00:49.710
Do you mean that all great murderers have been insane?

01:00:50.110 --> 01:00:51.280
Bet your sweet life.

01:00:51.930 --> 01:00:53.850
You think the Borgias were normal?

01:00:55.220 --> 01:00:55.940
Dr. Crippen.

01:00:55.940 --> 01:00:59.320
There was a saint and devil rolled into one.

01:01:00.570 --> 01:01:10.590
Landrew, the blue beard, Jack the Ripper, our own gangsters, Legs Diamond, Babyface Nelson, Dillinger, Paranoiax, all of them.

01:01:12.190 --> 01:01:16.920
Someday we'll have sense enough to train the mind as we train the body from birth.

01:01:17.570 --> 01:01:20.270
And they won't need men like me, and that'll be all right, too.

01:01:21.870 --> 01:01:26.100
What sort of job is this, anyway? Hunting down a madman.

01:01:28.320 --> 01:01:30.000
I'm all wound up.

01:01:30.960 --> 01:01:32.160
I guess I must be tired.

01:01:33.070 --> 01:01:34.570
Well, let's call it the night, shall we?

01:01:35.290 --> 01:01:36.400
You coming, Marlowe?

01:01:37.620 --> 01:01:38.280
Carol's waiting.

01:01:40.390 --> 01:01:40.730
Yes.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:04.240
Look, you run along. I'll be right with you.

01:02:04.240 --> 01:02:07.720
Don't tell Carol. You'd only be upset.

01:02:07.720 --> 01:02:23.330
Gosh, Chief, I've been looking all over the place for you.

01:02:23.330 --> 01:02:25.690
We've got to go to Philadelphia. It's a Vanzelli case.

01:02:25.690 --> 01:02:28.190
The Commissioner wants us to go right away. He's sure...

01:02:28.190 --> 01:02:29.410
What's the matter, Chief?

01:02:30.410 --> 01:02:31.930
Oh, the Vancelli case, what about it?

01:02:31.950 --> 01:02:33.470
Well, we've only got 20 minutes to get the train.

01:02:33.920 --> 01:02:35.150
No, I can't, I can't go.

01:02:35.350 --> 01:02:36.330
But orders is orders.

01:02:37.430 --> 01:02:39.160
Well, I suppose so.

01:02:40.190 --> 01:02:43.170
Carol, I'll try to be back by tomorrow afternoon.

01:02:43.920 --> 01:02:46.600
I want you to promise me that you won't do anything until then.

01:02:46.930 --> 01:02:48.140
But there's so much to do.

01:02:48.140 --> 01:02:49.840
Step on it, Chief, and we'll miss that train.

01:02:49.840 --> 01:02:50.720
Yes, yes, Tom.

01:02:51.090 --> 01:02:53.190
Remember, you're not to do anything until I get back.

01:02:53.750 --> 01:02:54.910
And take care of yourself.

01:02:56.140 --> 01:03:00.000
Oh, Mr. Marlowe, you'd better see a doctor about those dizzy spirits.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:06.340
- Goodbye, Carol. - Goodbye.

01:03:06.340 --> 01:03:14.860
- Miss Montero, please. - Miss Montero? Certainly.

01:03:14.860 --> 01:03:16.870
Oh, she left.

01:03:16.870 --> 01:03:21.490
Left? No, it's only 7:30.

01:03:21.490 --> 01:03:29.280
She took the 7 o'clock plane. You wrong?

01:03:32.620 --> 01:03:41.220
- No, thank you.

01:03:41.220 --> 01:03:48.830
- Chicago and the same in Pittsburgh.

01:03:48.830 --> 01:03:50.630
Every time I say I'm going to leave her,

01:03:50.630 --> 01:03:52.760
one of these days I will.

01:03:52.760 --> 01:03:54.320
- A taxi. - Yes, madame.

01:04:08.220 --> 01:04:09.420
I know you'll adore it.

01:04:09.770 --> 01:04:11.430
It does something very special for you.

01:04:11.620 --> 01:04:13.450
Thank you so much, Madame Patricia.

01:04:14.130 --> 01:04:15.230
Goodbye, Mrs. Witherspoon.

01:04:15.330 --> 01:04:15.790
Au revoir.

01:04:19.190 --> 01:04:23.820
I found it.

01:04:24.320 --> 01:04:26.920
This is the one Montero wore in the Chicka Chick number, isn't it?

01:04:27.100 --> 01:04:27.880
Sure, that's it.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:33.250
- Which one of your girls made it? - We had those two girls for years.

01:04:33.300 --> 01:04:37.720
Oh, my God. It's ridiculous to suggest it was copied here.

01:04:37.980 --> 01:04:41.100
Please, I'd be so grateful if I could see her.

01:04:41.200 --> 01:04:51.190
- Come in. - Yes, Madam Ketisha.

01:04:51.290 --> 01:05:00.000
- Remember Montero? - Yes.

01:05:00.060 --> 01:05:05.190
- Oh, I'd never do a thing like that. - I believe you. There, you see?

01:05:05.190 --> 01:05:11.080
Please forgive me for asking, but if you can tell me anything at all about it,

01:05:11.080 --> 01:05:15.330
you see, a man is going to die, unless you...

01:05:15.330 --> 01:05:21.910
- I'm sorry. I just can't tell you anything. - Thanks, Caden. That's all.

01:05:21.910 --> 01:05:29.900
- Poor kid.

01:05:30.920 --> 01:05:31.680
You're all in.

01:05:32.330 --> 01:05:33.730
How about going home, Carol?

01:05:38.030 --> 01:05:43.780
I, did you say a man's life?

01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:45.840
I mean, what is that to do with the hat?

01:05:46.160 --> 01:05:47.620
What are you driving at, Peyton?

01:05:48.510 --> 01:05:54.940
Well, I copied the hat.

01:05:57.420 --> 01:05:57.980
Thank you.

01:05:58.140 --> 01:05:59.860
Thank you so much for telling me.

01:06:01.630 --> 01:06:05.460
- You little rat! - She gave me 50 dollars to copy it for her.

01:06:05.460 --> 01:06:09.200
- Who is she? - She's one of our regular customers, Miss Terry.

01:06:09.200 --> 01:06:12.200
She saw a sketch of Monteiro's hat, liked it.

01:06:12.200 --> 01:06:14.160
We'll talk about that later, young lady.

01:06:14.160 --> 01:06:20.350
Sit down here and write the name and address.

01:06:20.350 --> 01:06:22.370
- Well? - Do as you're told.

01:06:46.830 --> 01:06:54.860
- That must be the house.

01:06:54.860 --> 01:06:56.680
- Kindly wait here, please. - Yes.

01:07:04.030 --> 01:07:07.280
I'm scared. I wonder what she's like.

01:07:08.760 --> 01:07:10.900
Jack, I can't believe it after all this time.

01:07:16.020 --> 01:07:18.700
How do you do?

01:07:18.900 --> 01:07:20.700
I'm Carol Richmond. This is Mr. Marlowe.

01:07:20.840 --> 01:07:21.320
How do you do?

01:07:21.440 --> 01:07:22.380
Miss Terry, we came to...

01:07:22.380 --> 01:07:23.460
I'm afraid you're making a mistake.

01:07:23.870 --> 01:07:25.790
I'm Dr. Chase. I'm looking out for Miss Terry.

01:07:26.870 --> 01:07:27.550
Is she ill?

01:07:28.060 --> 01:07:29.910
Yes. I'm a consultant on the case.

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:34.760
- Is it that serious? - Oh, there's nothing wrong with her physically.

01:07:34.760 --> 01:07:38.420
She collapsed last April after her fiancé died.

01:07:38.420 --> 01:07:43.970
She must have absolute quiet.

01:07:43.970 --> 01:07:47.070
I can't go away without talking to her.

01:07:47.070 --> 01:07:51.980
I've been looking for her for months.

01:07:51.980 --> 01:07:55.110
You're all worn out, aren't you?

01:07:55.110 --> 01:07:58.250
Perhaps if you tell me.

01:07:58.250 --> 01:08:00.000
Someone is going to be executed for a crime.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:03.330
He has a perfect alibi. He spent the evening with Miss Terry.

01:08:03.330 --> 01:08:05.330
She's the only one who can save him.

01:08:05.330 --> 01:08:08.720
Please, can't we see her?

01:08:08.720 --> 01:08:14.890
Come with me.

01:08:14.890 --> 01:08:21.380
It's better if Miss Richmond goes in alone.

01:08:21.380 --> 01:08:23.910
I'm afraid both of you might be too much for her.

01:08:23.910 --> 01:08:26.980
Yes.

01:08:30.410 --> 01:08:33.060
Keep your fingers crossed.

01:08:33.630 --> 01:08:36.970
And remember, you mustn't let her get too excited.

01:08:37.210 --> 01:08:46.580
I promise, you may go.

01:08:49.620 --> 01:08:55.160
- I'm here to see you. - Hello, Miss Terry.

01:08:55.710 --> 01:08:58.680
And dear, Miss Richmond wants to have a little talk with you.

01:09:01.530 --> 01:09:05.490
- I've been sick, but I'm better now.

01:09:05.490 --> 01:09:06.990
- Of course you are.

01:09:06.990 --> 01:09:09.150
Now then I'm going to leave you and Miss Richmond alone.

01:09:09.150 --> 01:09:11.800
- No, Helen, please don't leave me.

01:09:11.800 --> 01:09:13.910
- Look at Miss Richmond.

01:09:13.910 --> 01:09:19.200
You're not afraid of her.

01:09:19.200 --> 01:09:23.160
That's right.

01:09:23.160 --> 01:09:25.620
- This is a lovely room.

01:09:25.620 --> 01:09:28.470
It was my grandmother's.

01:09:28.470 --> 01:09:30.000
She lived in this house.

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:41.120
all her life. She was very happy here. She married the man she loved. I'll never marry.

01:09:44.300 --> 01:09:59.080
Are you married? No. You're in love? Yes. He was only sick two days. He'd never been sick before.

01:10:01.500 --> 01:10:03.500
She was always so full of life.

01:10:03.500 --> 01:10:07.000
We were to be married the following week.

01:10:07.000 --> 01:10:09.730
I had my trousseau bought,

01:10:09.730 --> 01:10:12.880
and a special dress and hat for the wedding.

01:10:12.880 --> 01:10:14.420
They must have been lovely.

01:10:14.420 --> 01:10:16.910
Do you still have them?

01:10:16.910 --> 01:10:21.570
I don't want to talk anymore.

01:10:21.570 --> 01:10:26.040
Can't I see them, Miss Terry?

01:10:26.040 --> 01:10:29.480
I don't want to talk anymore.

01:11:42.600 --> 01:11:46.040
It's all right, Anne. You can show it to me.

01:12:03.610 --> 01:12:05.940
He loved it.

01:12:05.940 --> 01:12:06.940
But he never saw it.

01:12:06.940 --> 01:12:09.360
Beautiful.

01:12:09.360 --> 01:12:12.840
I wish I had a hat like that.

01:12:12.840 --> 01:12:14.410
Hair.

01:12:14.410 --> 01:12:15.410
My hair's no good this way.

01:12:15.410 --> 01:12:17.130
May I borrow it?

01:12:17.130 --> 01:12:19.130
I'll bring it back to you.

01:12:19.130 --> 01:12:28.200
Oh, you want a word for him.

01:12:28.200 --> 01:12:29.890
Is he nice, the man you love?

01:12:31.280 --> 01:12:46.570
- Yes. Take it. I don't want to. He's dead. He's dead!

01:13:10.010 --> 01:13:12.020
- Have I been asleep long?

01:13:12.020 --> 01:13:14.270
- Yes, we're halfway home.

01:13:14.270 --> 01:13:16.920
- Oh, I can hardly wait to tell Burgess.

01:13:16.920 --> 01:13:20.780
Last night, everything seemed so hopeless.

01:13:20.780 --> 01:13:22.870
What's the matter?

01:13:22.870 --> 01:13:24.710
- Oh, nothing.

01:13:24.710 --> 01:13:26.470
- Do you want me to drive?

01:13:26.470 --> 01:13:30.000
- No, no, I'll be all right.

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:31.830
a headache.

01:13:32.850 --> 01:13:33.850
Well, it's no wonder

01:13:33.850 --> 01:13:35.090
you haven't eaten all day.

01:13:35.800 --> 01:13:36.580
It's my fault.

01:13:36.640 --> 01:13:37.440
We should have stopped.

01:13:39.600 --> 01:13:42.260
You've been awfully nice to me, Jack.

01:13:42.960 --> 01:13:43.860
I don't know

01:13:43.860 --> 01:13:45.040
what I would have done without you.

01:13:49.350 --> 01:13:51.260
Well, let's stop over here

01:13:51.260 --> 01:13:52.060
and call Burgess.

01:13:55.480 --> 01:13:58.560
I'll only be a moment.

01:13:59.040 --> 01:14:00.000
No, you stay here.

01:14:00.030 --> 01:14:01.510
I'll do it.

01:14:53.130 --> 01:14:54.280
Is he back?

01:14:54.280 --> 01:14:55.280
No, not yet.

01:14:55.280 --> 01:14:59.050
Well, then we'd better go to headquarters right away and wait for him.

01:14:59.050 --> 01:15:00.000
I left word for him.

01:15:00.190 --> 01:15:07.170
meet us at my place. We can all have a drink and celebrate. All right. Oh, I can hardly

01:15:07.170 --> 01:15:21.280
wait to tell him the news. When I first came to New York, I lived a whole week on nothing

01:15:21.280 --> 01:15:27.240
but sandwiches. Then when I got my first job, I went out and I ate the biggest dinner I

01:15:27.240 --> 01:15:30.000
could find. I was so happy.

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:32.100
- That's the way I feel tonight.

01:15:32.100 --> 01:15:35.210
- Burgess should be here by now.

01:15:35.210 --> 01:15:36.600
- Yes.

01:15:36.600 --> 01:15:39.090
- I can hardly wait to tell him.

01:15:39.090 --> 01:15:40.580
He'll be so excited.

01:15:40.580 --> 01:15:42.700
Jack, isn't it wonderful?

01:15:42.700 --> 01:15:44.420
The silly hat.

01:15:44.420 --> 01:15:48.710
- Well, save Scott, Burgess can reopen the case.

01:15:48.710 --> 01:15:54.570
- Hmm, looks rather smart.

01:15:54.570 --> 01:15:57.460
- You know, I've never heard you laugh before.

01:15:57.460 --> 01:16:00.000
- And then Burgess will find the murderer.

01:16:01.500 --> 01:16:04.620
I want to hear the court sentence him as they sentence Scott.

01:16:05.390 --> 01:16:08.350
I hate him, don't I?

01:16:08.350 --> 01:16:09.560
I hate him.

01:16:14.250 --> 01:16:15.430
Is that starting up again?

01:16:17.550 --> 01:16:18.870
Why don't you lie down, Jack?

01:16:19.050 --> 01:16:20.210
Oh, I'll be all right.

01:16:20.330 --> 01:16:21.110
No, no, I insist.

01:16:21.150 --> 01:16:21.950
I do as I say.

01:16:22.430 --> 01:16:24.350
Come on, get some rest before Burgess comes.

01:16:25.110 --> 01:16:26.030
Oh, I'm a mess.

01:16:26.150 --> 01:16:27.390
I think I'd better freshen up a bit.

01:16:27.810 --> 01:16:28.350
All right.

01:16:28.760 --> 01:16:30.000
Now, you'll get some sleep, won't you?

01:17:39.980 --> 01:17:42.450
- Police headquarters, quick.

01:17:42.450 --> 01:17:43.760
- Police headquarters.

01:17:43.760 --> 01:17:47.600
- Inspector Burgess's office, hurry.

01:17:47.600 --> 01:17:50.510
- That extension is, will you wait?

01:17:50.510 --> 01:17:52.010
- Yes, I'll hold on, but hurry.

01:18:35.340 --> 01:18:53.380
- Please, come here.

01:18:53.380 --> 01:18:56.040
- Don't I look better?

01:18:56.040 --> 01:18:57.290
I thought you'd be asleep.

01:18:57.290 --> 01:19:00.000
- Until I turn it out, please.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:21.940
Hurts my eye, chokes me, right here beside me, head's bursting, it's on fire.

01:19:23.040 --> 01:19:24.560
Give me your hand.

01:19:32.840 --> 01:19:40.710
Feels good, quiet here, so far away from everything.

01:19:40.710 --> 01:19:45.460
I never liked cities, noise, confusion, dirt.

01:19:45.460 --> 01:19:48.300
And the people in it, they hate me

01:19:48.300 --> 01:19:51.580
because I'm different from them.

01:19:51.580 --> 01:19:56.160
I don't belong here, neither do you.

01:19:56.160 --> 01:19:59.250
It isn't fair for someone like you to be suffering.

01:20:00.350 --> 01:20:01.550
You should be so happy.

01:20:03.920 --> 01:20:05.300
You'd never come to New York.

01:20:06.210 --> 01:20:07.250
Never met Scott.

01:20:09.240 --> 01:20:11.100
The world's full of men like him.

01:20:11.180 --> 01:20:13.840
You can buy nice stupid people a dime a dozen.

01:20:33.520 --> 01:20:36.580
She was sitting at her dressing table, just as you're sitting there.

01:20:37.330 --> 01:20:39.920
Only she wasn't frightened, as you are.

01:20:40.940 --> 01:20:42.320
Marcella was never frightened.

01:20:44.350 --> 01:20:45.490
I said you'd better hurry.

01:20:46.200 --> 01:20:47.640
She leaves in an hour.

01:20:49.970 --> 01:20:53.170
And then she told me she'd never had any intention of going with me.

01:20:53.230 --> 01:20:54.950
She was just amusing herself.

01:20:57.420 --> 01:21:00.000
I saw myself.

01:21:01.720 --> 01:21:25.930
- I don't want anything to interfere with my work.

01:21:25.930 --> 01:21:30.000
You can't afford to let them get your gifts.

01:21:30.440 --> 01:21:34.920
I saw him with that woman, then she slipped away from me and I had to bribe the others.

01:21:34.920 --> 01:21:40.310
They think I took the boat that night, but I didn't.

01:21:40.310 --> 01:21:43.840
I went aboard all right, but I left before she sailed.

01:21:43.840 --> 01:21:48.820
SS Volkania, August 2nd, 8:30 p.m.

01:21:48.820 --> 01:21:50.280
Ha! That idiot!

01:21:50.280 --> 01:21:52.660
I flew to Havana, caught the boat there.

01:21:52.660 --> 01:21:56.530
Ah, he never thought of that. That was too clever for him.

01:21:56.530 --> 01:22:00.000
Scott, how could he?

01:22:00.000 --> 01:22:07.920
- I'm fond of Scott, we're friends.

01:22:07.920 --> 01:22:11.020
But what's his life compared to mine?

01:22:11.020 --> 01:22:15.770
A mediocre engineer working in sewers, drain pipes, faucets.

01:22:15.770 --> 01:22:21.870
What's any life compared to mine?

01:22:21.870 --> 01:22:26.450
I asked you not to interfere, but you wouldn't listen.

01:22:26.450 --> 01:22:30.000
It'd be so easy.

01:22:31.600 --> 01:22:34.000
- No one will question me.

01:22:34.000 --> 01:22:48.450
They'll say it's just another suicide.

01:22:48.450 --> 01:22:49.790
- Don't you see?

01:22:49.790 --> 01:22:50.870
After me there'll be others.

01:22:50.870 --> 01:22:53.670
You'll have to go on killing, on and on until they catch you.

01:22:53.670 --> 01:22:54.530
- No.

01:22:54.530 --> 01:22:56.610
- I won't be the last, there'll be others after me.

01:22:56.610 --> 01:22:57.460
- No.

01:22:57.460 --> 01:23:00.000
- You can't help yourself because you're mad, mad, mad!

01:24:19.070 --> 01:24:20.070
- Good morning, Mary.

01:24:20.070 --> 01:24:21.070
- Good morning, Miss Richmond.

01:24:21.070 --> 01:24:26.180
Good morning.

01:24:26.180 --> 01:24:27.170
- Good morning, Carol.

01:24:27.170 --> 01:24:29.090
Hello, Kansas.

01:24:29.090 --> 01:24:29.910
- Well?

01:24:30.440 --> 01:24:31.640
How do we like the new office?

01:24:31.860 --> 01:24:32.650
It's not bad.

01:24:34.080 --> 01:24:35.060
Oh, 9.30 already.

01:24:35.260 --> 01:24:36.060
I've got to rush.

01:24:36.700 --> 01:24:38.460
I'm seeing Kepler about the chemicals plant.

01:24:38.950 --> 01:24:39.930
When will you be back?

01:24:40.280 --> 01:24:41.170
Might take all day.

01:24:41.550 --> 01:24:43.250
If I'm not back by 6, don't wait.

01:24:46.160 --> 01:24:48.340
By the way, I left instructions on the dictaphone.

01:24:48.910 --> 01:24:50.170
You'll take care of them for me, won't you?

01:24:50.840 --> 01:24:51.920
Goodbye, Kansas.

01:24:54.130 --> 01:24:55.900
So long, Burgess.

01:24:56.000 --> 01:24:56.480
Goodbye, Henderson.

01:24:59.300 --> 01:25:00.000
Oh, quite as old.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:02.020
he owes you a great deal, Carol.

01:25:02.020 --> 01:25:07.840
I did it because I wanted to.

01:25:07.840 --> 01:25:11.650
Will I have to appear at the investigation tomorrow?

01:25:11.650 --> 01:25:13.570
No, it's only a formality.

01:25:13.570 --> 01:25:15.390
The evidence shows that Marlow O'Fell

01:25:15.390 --> 01:25:17.390
attempting to escape onto the ledge.

01:25:17.390 --> 01:25:19.600
I've got to be off.

01:25:19.600 --> 01:25:21.600
I have to be down at the court at 10 o'clock.

01:25:21.600 --> 01:25:24.950
Well, good-bye, Carol.

01:25:24.950 --> 01:25:25.800
Good-bye, Burgess.

01:25:40.940 --> 01:25:44.960
Membership to the Architects and Engineers Association and call Mason and Fowler, the

01:25:44.960 --> 01:25:47.360
contractors, and make an appointment with them for tomorrow morning.

01:25:50.000 --> 01:26:00.000
Uh-uh-uh, don't hang tonight, next night, and then every night.

01:26:01.540 --> 01:26:03.010
Every night.
